## What the MIT grant above does and does not cover

The MIT license above applies to the **source code** of this repository: the
TypeScript, React components, build plugins, test suites and configuration.

It does **not** apply to the written and creative content, which is
© 2026 Zach Scheffler, all rights reserved:

- Prose and written content — the case studies under `src/pages/*CaseStudy.tsx`,
  the CV text and biography in `src/content/cv.ts`, and the copy throughout
  `src/content/` and the page components.
- The curriculum vitae and its generated PDF (`Zach-Scheffler-CV.pdf`).
- Images and brand assets, including `public/og-image.png`.
- Music, audio recordings and the recording credits in `src/content/work.ts`.

Reuse the code freely. Please don't republish the writing, the CV or the music
as your own.

## Third-party data and assets

This repository includes or refers to material owned by others, under their own
terms — not under the grant above:

- `public/data/spotify_songs.csv` — the 2020 TidyTuesday Spotify sample.
- `public/data/egmd.json` — derived from the Expanded Groove MIDI Dataset
  (E-GMD v1.0.0, Google Magenta).
- Ethnomusicological citations in `src/content/atlasCitations.ts` — titles and
  bibliographic references to third-party scholarship, cited but not licensed
  here.
- Basemap tiles are served by Esri and are subject to Esri's terms.
